            "subject": "LU-12669 lov: peer-relative deadline for EC raid set reads"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-15 08:03:44.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-15 08:27:11.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-12669 lov: split EC reads at a raid set parity cannot cover",
        "message": "LU-12669 lov: split EC reads at a raid set parity cannot cover\n\nA read of an EC file that touches a raid set with more dead stripes\nthan its parity can stand in for waits for their OSTs, even for the\ndead stripes of raid sets that parity could rebuild, so the whole read\nwaits for every dead OST.  Reconstructing the whole read instead fails\non that set with -EIO, as a CIT_EC_RD cycle covers all raid sets of a\nrow at once.\n\nStop the read where the first raid set of the other kind starts, and\nrestart the rest there: a reconstruction stops before a set that\ncannot be rebuilt (cl_io::ci_ec_split), and ll_file_io_generic()\nrestarts the rest as a CIT_READ, which waits for that set; a read that\nwaits stops before a set that can be rebuilt.  A failed direct read\nwhose DIO state is already freed keeps restarting as CIT_EC_RD.  A\nlarge read() across many rows with alternating raid sets uses three\nrestarts per row, as going back to reconstruction restarts once more\nas CIT_READ and then as CIT_EC_RD, so it returns short after about 333\nsuch rows, once RETRY_ATTEMPTS restarts are used up.\n\nAdd sanity-ec test_77o, which reads two rows and brings back only the\nraid set that cannot be rebuilt, and checks that the read completes\nwith the data stripe of the other set still down.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5 ltvm,llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I21a023db83276919086acb9bc75cbf3d733ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
